            <ArticleTitle>Interventional treatment of giant pseudoaneurysm with subsequent decompression of internal mammaria bypass.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>525-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of a 38-year-old patient with angina after direct current (DC) cardioversion. The patient's medical history included documented coronary heart disease with interventional treatment of the LAD and RCA followed by emergency CABG 6 months ago. On recent admission, the coronary angiography revealed a giant pseudoaneurysm of the left descending coronary artery complicated by compression of LIMA. The pseudoaneurysm was successfully treated with three stent grafts.</AbstractText>
